WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
Glacier Time Machine: Muir Inlet, Alaska on the real Copernicus elevation model

2
00:00:03.004 --> 00:00:12.007
Fly up the inlet on the real elevation model, draped with a 2024 Sentinel-2 image — no vertical exaggeration

3
00:00:12.008 --> 00:00:13.510
Skip any cinematic from the first frame (Esc)

4
00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:19.014
Same place, different time: the USGS repeat photographs, 1941 to 2004

5
00:00:19.014 --> 00:00:26.017
The glacier retreated more than 3 km in nine years — and more than 7 km by 2004

6
00:00:26.017 --> 00:00:31.022
Module 3 opens on the dated ice fronts: step between the photo years

7
00:00:31.022 --> 00:00:37.524
The 3D front sits only at dated anchors; the movement in between is labelled illustrative, not measured

8
00:00:37.524 --> 00:00:42.027
Draw the measuring line on the real terrain; Check measurement grades the line you drew

9
00:00:42.027 --> 00:00:46.528
What came next: succession after the ice, with the evidence sorted for you to judge

10
00:00:46.528 --> 00:00:51.030
Every claim shows its source; the past-year ground colours are labelled illustrative

11
00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:55.035
Every task also works in text mode, with the same data

12
00:00:55.035 --> 00:00:58.037
Free, no account, no tracking: immersive-learning-showcase.vercel.app
